**Theorem 22.4 (termination and exact recognized image).**
Definition 22.3 terminates on every finite rational input and accepts
exactly $\operatorname{im}F_{\rm blk}$, returning its unique block
Time. On the corresponding serial realizations, equality of settled
term/field is exactly equality of blocks and gaps, with only the
within-block permutations forgotten.

Proof. Every inverse exists rationally by (2.3).
A positive nonzero inverse loop which never reaches a zero or rejects
would stay in the unit cube, while
$\|T^{-r}y\|_\infty\ge\lambda^{-r}\|y\|_\infty$ eventually exceeds
one. Thus each loop terminates. Every accepted block strictly reduces
material size, so there are finitely many collapses. The final positive
scalar doubles until reaching or exceeding one in finitely many steps.
All parsing, support and finite exact comparison tests terminate.
This proves totality even for off-image rational inputs.

Every actual block history passes by Theorem 22.2 and its positivity
induction. Its inner counters are positive and its two endpoint gaps
are permitted to be zero. For soundness, an accepting chain gives the
alpha equation and finitely many equations (22.2). Its parsed
comparisons define actual independent nonempty blocks on each
predecessor. The inner-counter condition gives exactly the positive
internal gaps of (22.1). Reading these equations forward therefore
constructs an actual member of $\mathcal H_{\rm blk}$ with the
accepted endpoint. Theorem 22.2 makes its certificate unique.

Each serial realization has that evaluated block/gap endpoint.
Equality of two endpoints forces the same decoded certificate.
Conversely identical blocks and gaps with different internal
enumerations have identical fields by Theorem 21.2.
This proves the exact kernel claim within this declared domain.
Literal earlier Growth replies can distinguish the two enumerations;
their erased journals are not part of this settled endpoint task.
$\square$

